  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment for young men and women through entrepreneurship, Value Chain Development, green enterprises, social enterprises and cooperatives  and business development programmes promoted</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to challenges arising from the growing refugee population in Egypt&#x2014;and their vulnerabilities and the pressures placed on host communities&#x2014;the Netherlands launched the PROSPECTS initiative, in partnership with the IFC, ILO, UNHCR, UNICEF, and the World Bank.
Building on a first phase concluding in December 2024, PROSPECTS Egypt will continue through 2027 to enhance living standards and inclusivity for refugees, asylum-seekers, and vulnerable host populations across Greater Cairo, Alexandria, and Damietta. The initiative centers on four key pillars:
- Expanding access to quality education, skills training, and learning opportunities for forcibly displaced persons (FDPs) and host communities (HCs).
- Strengthening livelihoods and economic prospects through entrepreneurship and dignified employment.
- Increasing government protection and fostering greater inclusion in local, community-based, and national social protection systems.
- Improving services, infrastructure, and information systems essential to FDPs and HCs.
The DECENT WORK FOR WOMEN project&#x2014;supported by EBRD&#x2014;enables employer organizations in Egypt, Tunisia, and Morocco to train their members, particularly women, for the green transition. Its curriculum spans green business innovation, certification, finance, and sector-specific guidance for women-led enterprises.
The PE4DW Egypt project, funded by the Italian Agency and implemented with Egypt&#x2019;s Ministry of Trade and Industry, supports productivity and decent work in the leather and marble sectors. It assists 200 SMEs in overcoming productivity barriers and improving working conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
